The formula's primary movement controls are mostly sound: sentence mean, long-sentence share and scene length all fall inside the accepted ranges. The largest drift is the narrow sentence spread, followed by the high paragraph mean and very easy readability estimate. This matches the reading experience only partly: the vocabulary and individual sentences are accessible, but the institutional concepts in chapter 17 remain cognitively dense. Raising syllable count merely to move Flesch would not improve the thirteen-year-old reading experience.

The six editorial placeholders are counted as ordinary prose by the documented method, so these figures describe the unrepaired draft. Re-run the same tool only after the protected text is restored and the targeted prose repair is complete.

