# Editorial review — Movement 003, chapters 13–19

## Review status and coverage

**Verdict: REPAIR before close.** The movement is structurally successful and the seven-chapter arc is complete, but it is not release-ready: six literal `[[TIER-B: ...]]` placeholders remain in the manuscript, one applicable protected line is paraphrased instead of reproduced verbatim, and one sentence contradicts the binding stake-mark ruling.

Coverage is limited to the seven supplied chapters, `chapter-13.md` through `chapter-19.md`, totaling 33,947 prose words. This is a fresh-context simulated reader review combined with an informed editorial/canon pass; it is neither a real human read nor a blind cold read, and it is not self-review of prose I drafted.

## Unscored reader response

Interest caught first on Karis and Brom claiming the road job with “Ours” (`chapter-13.md:41-45`), then locked in when the visible pack changes from five to eight (`chapter-14.md:269-281`) and Vastin steps into the road after apologizing (`chapter-15.md:21-35`). The cut is the movement's strongest sequence: its terrain, doctrine, error, adaptation and costs remain legible while revealing character.

Interest slipped during the densest run of office procedure in chapter 17 (`chapter-17.md:107-149`). The logic is sound, but routing heads, survey abstracts, missing names, form redesign and schedule classification arrive in one sustained sequence. A fluent thirteen-year-old can follow each sentence while still losing which discovery matters most. The unresolved editorial markers in chapters 16–19 then break immersion outright.

Vastin matters most in this movement. His inability to watch another person be bitten, the badly placed wall, the injury, his exact obedience to a warning he refused to promise, and Seln's first lesson turn him from an office into a person without excusing what he was. Seln's decision to give Cael the date without controlling its meaning is the strongest secondary beat.

I expect the next event to test the written station promise as the group enters Treswick, followed by the meeting with Cleon and the attempt to read the marks. I would continue. The last image—Cael choosing the lowest wall while the station light remains above him—creates clean forward pressure (`chapter-19.md:245-289`).

