   209	They drilled him for the last of the light, and it was Lira who did most of it. She had taught a boy from another crew to wait for a pole, and she went at an Archmarshal in the same fashion and with no more ceremony, walking backward before him down forty yards of rutted road with her right hand going. He stood for the flat hand and came on for the two fingers; and when the fist was thrown out to the left he looked left, and found a thorn-bush, and regarded it with great attention.
   210	
   211	"That's well enough," she said, low. "Now look at yourself. No, don't move. Look where you are."
   212	
