   254	
   255	With the dark, the quietest of the ten came up in Cael to the height of his knees, and he held it there, as he did at every dusk. A healer sat on the next stone with her sleeves down. She had looked at a stiff leg four times since the bread was cut, and Tide, the tenth, lay as still in him as she sat, and for the same reason: nobody had been asked.
   256	
   257	Brom had brought seven bowls out of the pannier, and nobody had seen him count. He filled the seventh with what there was, which was cold barley and a heel of cheese, and set it on a stone; and Vastin thanked him by name. A little afterward a copper lay on that stone beside the empty bowl. Brom looked at it for a while, and left it where it was.
