   259	Cael wrote by feel, on his knee.
   260	
   261	*Two hundred and seventy-eighth day. A halting-ground on the border road, eleven miles from the river. A slip taken at the plank: a clearance, the cut below the shoulder hold, twenty. Five hands. Pike has a sixth line on it for the healer, of her own road. Vastin walks behind us. He was not asked, and he was not told no. He has the four hands, and he knows where a post stands. He says that he cannot promise to watch one of us bitten, and I believe him. The rope on the far bank was three-strand; Brom would not have it. In hand, a hundred and eighteen.*
   262	
   263	*I ruled on a job. I have still not touched the page.*
   264	
   265	*Deployment since the Line: thirty.*

