 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Chapter 16 — A Month
     2	
     3	Oryn came up the cut on the dry edge, at the pace that she kept for a gate with a bell ringing, and she stopped at her stride and a half and looked the whole of it over before she spoke.
     4	
     5	It took her three breaths, in which Cael saw her eyes go to five grey shapes, and leave them, since they were past her trade. They went to a girl who was wiping a long knife on a tuft of bents with her left hand; to a small man who had come out of the broken ice wet to the shins and was looking at nothing; to a large one sitting on a stone with his foot out. They came to Cael, and passed over him as they passed over a gatepost. Then they stopped.
     6	
     7	"That's first," she said.
     8	
     9	Vastin had straightened. He had his back to the south bank and both hands on the stick, and below his right knee the brown frieze was black and wet from the joint to the boot.
    10	
    11	"I am in no immediate—"
    12	
    13	"I'll say when it's my turn to be told." She did not go nearer. "Three days ago, at a board, I opened my mouth about that leg, and you answered a thing that I'd not yet put. You said that you offered it to nobody. So I said that I still hadn't asked, and I let it lie, since that's my rule and I keep it." She pushed her left sleeve a little higher. "This is the asking. There are teeth in that, and under the teeth a joint that's been walked three hundred miles and then stood on by eight of those. I want my hands on it. And I want two fingers on your wrist while I'm there, to learn what's left in you. May I?"
    14	
    15	He did not answer at once.
    16	
    17	Cael watched him look for the form of it. A man who had spent his life granting leave, and refusing it, under his hand and a seal, was being asked a plain thing by a woman on a road who had no office to ask it from. He looked at her bare forearms. He looked, for an instant, at the five who stood about him, and it came to Cael that he was waiting to hear whether any of them would answer for him.
    18	
    19	Nobody did.
    20	
