    19	A date read once, by lamplight, over another person's shoulder, in another person's pencil, at the end of such a day, by a man who would have paid a year's wages to find it otherwise, was not a finding. He might have taken one figure for another. So might she, for all that she never did. He might, after fifteen years of files, have laid the wrong day at the head of the right one. There were three places where it could have slipped, and he had spent two days on a road going over each of the three.
