editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-05.md:93:There were five people in a room that had been built for sacks, and the only sound in it was the fire on the other side of the wall. Cael looked at two strips of brass. One had come from Ternhall in a researcher's coat, and one from Denvash in a bag, and he had laid both of them along a pencil line at a hearth thirty-seven days ago and found them true. He felt the cold of that yard in his stomach.
