editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md:15:"The third is a sheet of paper which reached my desk by mistake. It had this town's name on it, and a board's; and where a crew's name should have stood, it had five strokes, and a count of six. I had not known where you were gone, and I had been at some pains not to learn. I knew of only one five who had gone that way. You shall have the sheet tonight; it is the last in what I carry."
