editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-63-Her voice had gone hard. She jerked her chin at Brom's back, at four yards of webbing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-64-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md:65:"It's why I asked you. A hundred and sixty-three days ago six people stood on a rim, over a place called the Stair, with crossbows. They'd cloths across their faces. No seals, no word, nothing you could have written down. One of them put a bolt in him. They knew which hole we were in before we'd climbed out of it." She leaned across the board. "You say nothing of yours crosses the Line. Something did."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-66-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-67-Vastin looked at the webbing for some time. It was the look that he had given a margin with a clerk's four lines folded inside it.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-79-"Then you showed them rightly. I could not have lifted that paper when I held the seal. I asked what would lift it, and the answer is that nothing will, short of the settling of his status; and his status can be settled only on a plate." For the first time since he sat down his eyes stayed on Cael a breath longer than they had stayed on the rest. "I say it so that nobody at this board supposes that a man's leaving his office has altered that instrument by a comma. I crossed a sill with nothing waiting for me on either side of it. Not one of you four could say as much of the way back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md-80-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-11.md:81:Cael had told a board that he would rule when the first boat was in, since a desk might have changed the price. The boat was in. He had the price now from the office that used to certify such things, and it was last year's price, to the copper. Nothing about it had altered but this: a second person had come to the same town's name, by another road, and had not known that it was already on their table.
