editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-12.md:85:He had put his thick finger down on the deal beside the page, not touching it, under two words. Cael did not need them pointed out. They were the name of a town, and the name of the part of it that lay lowest. A small pale woman had said both at a board nine days ago, with her palm on a strip of oilcloth; and at noon a man who had never heard of her map had said the first of them again.
