editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-12.md-263-Oryn had stood by the hinges through the whole of it, with her sleeves down. She had heard a town named at noon, and she had read a page tonight from where she stood, since her eyes were as good as her hands. Cael saw her look at that page, and at the hand that lay beside it, and he saw her mouth open.
