editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-1-### Coordinator rulings (binding)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-2-- **Entry seam with Movement 2 ratified** (Sol plan audit): day 278 at Lowmarch; purse 118; deployment thirty; the papers with Karis; Vastin off the sheet and following; the ferry for people only; the cordage on the western bank **refused as three-strand** — sixty yards of four-strand are still owed to the ferryman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-3-- **The slip:** *Clearance. The cut below the shoulder hold, on the border road, two days west.* Twenty. "Ours" (Karis), "Ours" (Brom); five hands; Pike's sixth line: *And a healer; of her own road; at her own price.* Brom holds the thumbed slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-4-- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTY-TWO**, both on the 279th at the cut: one grain of Ember at the mark (thirty-one; the heat came home along the left arm) and one Wind burst **away**, ten strides, to the north bank inside the wall (thirty-two). Pressure, Anchor, Edge, Storm and the read refused there. Shadow held, twice and sealed; Tide unused; no self-reading; Oryn has not read Cael. **Ten fragments: nothing came of standing two feet from the wall; the eleventh has not come.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-5-- **The cut (the author's staging stands; BOOK_MAP §8 allows it).** A hundred strides, a stride of ice down the middle, scree on the south, a low north bank, the sink fifty-five yards below it. Eight hounds (five seen, three hidden). The den had learned the road: it runs to where a declaration ENDS. Karis, Oryn and the mule were at the foot; Vastin, a stride behind Brom, stepped out and **declared Iron Wall** — a plane across the road from a line struck with his stick, wall to wall, two feet from Cael, rooted (he may not lift a foot), loud, spending him to the floor. Brom's rock (twice), Lira's knife with the left hand holding, Seln in the heap; five dead; **three went through the rotten ice of the sink and did not come up**. Costs: Brom's right foot (two toes, ten days from the 279th); **Vastin's right knee** (four holes shut by Oryn after "May I?" / "Yes"; the joint bound with laths; **a month** from the 279th: stick, no kneeling, no running, no wall). Karis's sixth line: *It goes to where a declaration ends, if it has learned that the declaring moves.* Twenty paid; **purse 138**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-6-- **Protected (speakers):** "Carters declare, on the ice." (the factor, unnamed, no pronoun); "It's clear because it's empty, not because it's safe," (Seln — the plan quotes only this clause; the source's fuller sentence contradicts the staging and was not restored); the wall lesson (Vastin) / "You do now," (Cael) / "I know fields…" (Vastin); the log verbatim.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-7-- **The spring (the 280th).** Six rows counted twice by two people. Five columns on every abstract: the day in the registry's reckoning; the station (eight points); the measure; *Instruments* ("Cord true. Edge true. Level true." on every line for six years); the anomaly (*Total*). **Karis matches FOUR sign-groups to the hide by their measures (three alike to the stride, one double) and gives no number of places; no fifth place is described** (held for the 298th). The measures have not changed in six years. The remark *Behaves as device. Cannot be.* stands in a ruled space on the Stair's sheet in the fourth row; **its hand is not identified**; the space for remarks is gone from the next year's printing. **The grade:** a ruled square at the head of every sheet with the same stroke and bar on all four matched places, drawn no larger on the place whose measure is double; in the field it is on stake thirty-two and on the fourth site's thirty-fours only. Karis: a class, unread; "Two copies of one ignorance." Nobody says who set it or why. Karis stopped her lamps sentence with the ruler line and did not finish it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-8-- **The date.** Seln drew the technician's sheet from the foot of the second row; the row counted a sheet short in Cael's hands; Seln set the sheet before him without a word. **Cael read the date and knew it for the day of his own Kindling** (the first line of his file). Only Cael and Seln know; neither has said or written it; neither knows what the other made of it; nobody has interpreted the sequence. Karis knows both have read the sheet. **No figures are printed, no span is computed, and there is NO second calendar** (the author's stations'-year offset was cut: the series calendar is the owner's). The sheet lies again at the foot of the second row.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md:9:- **Vastin's three reflexes** (a directive; a classification; "This has to go up") and **the first thing Seln ever taught anyone:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." / "Draft nothing. Just look." **Cleon** was named for the first time (Vastin: "Treswick,"; Karis: "The archive under it. Cleon."; Cael: "Who's Cleon?"); OWNER-pending #52 verbatim, as Karis's own rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-10-- **The fork (the 280th evening; the 281st).** Oryn: "I'm not an archive person."; her past (a house for the sick in a city inside the Line; the column for the patient's tier; a woman from the river sheds whom she mended off the sheet; she walked out of a gate and has not been through one since — the author's, kept); "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second."; Seln's "Three weeks"; **the station term, written in the log and read back (verbatim)**; she priced all six, Vastin as long as the rest; "That's on me. It's the one thing I'm walking up that road owing, and I'll pay it." (the reading she has not given Cael); "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it."; "Not the steps," … "Not the square." She went north with the brown mule, her linen and the crossbow with its one bolt: five gates, the ford, Millrace in three weeks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-11-- **Loads from the fork:** boxes on Brom (good shoulder), Lira (both arms) and Cael; Karis the flat and the hide; **Vastin took up the tarred kit case unasked** and has walked beside Cael since the rise. Brom carries Oryn's empty bowl.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-12-- **The rise (the 281st, near noon):** Treswick a day's walk off — a bluff in a river loop, three walls in tiers, a pale steady light on the crown that Cael does not look at. **Cael laid his hand on the page** (the author's; kept); it stays in its oilcloth in Karis's coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/LEDGER-RULINGS.md-13-- **Teague** was at the landing with forty sacks on the 278th; his term stands; the tall man has he/his. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 34,000.
