editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-6-- **Deployment and fragments:** every use in earnest in ch13–19 (the Wind burst at the cut; anything else), every refusal, every log line; state the count at movement end. Shadow sealed; Anchor's count; Tide unused; no self-read; Oryn does not read Cael.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-7-- **The spring (the 280th).** Three readers (Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure). "Behaves as device. Cannot be." — whose remark, on which paper, and does anyone interpret it? Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule and never finishes it. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites in the office's SHEETS, the fourth's twice the size (the field stakes carry it on thirty-two and thirty-four only — coordinator ruling after Movement 1); it stays unread; nobody says who graded the sites or why. **The date:** the second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands; Seln sets the technician's sheet before him without a word; Cael reads a Compact date and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. **No figures are printed (OWNER #60), no span of years is computed (#18), nothing is said or written, and nobody interprets the sequence.** Flag any line that prints a number for the date, counts years, has anyone say the sum, or joins the date to the layer "running". This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone (the "Draft nothing. Just look." exchange): confirm he taught nothing earlier in the movement. Seln's locked case stays shut.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-8-- **Seln's cutaway (~1,800):** he does the sum and decides to set the sheet before Cael; he does not theorize about the deep layer. Check it gives no figure and no interpretation.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-9-- **Vastin:** no age; walks at the back; not on the sheet; learning the silent doctrine, not drilling under a wall; never framed as joining; does not learn what Cael carries. What does he see at the cut and the spring that he could not have seen before?
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-10-- **Oryn and the fork (the 280th evening, the 281st first light):** her terms; the city she left; the column for the patient's tier; "Three weeks."; the station term (verbatim, asked, written, read back); she prices everyone, Vastin included, none lower than the rest; the mule goes north with her; the fork is on this side of the long rise and her condition was first written "at the fork above Millrace" in Book 7 — check against locked Book 7. Pike's sixth line for the healer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-11-- **Teague:** where is he on the 278th (the plan left it open; forty sacks of salt; a block on the second ledge of the cold road)? The tall man has he/his. No crew member named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-12-- **Money:** from 118 marks: the slip pays twenty; any purchase (the cordage and the rope debt to the ferryman — is it paid before they leave Lowmarch? the broker's price?); the purse at movement end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-13-- **Calendar:** each day 278–281 against BOOK_MAP §6; "two days west"; Treswick first seen from the top of the rise on the 281st, with the pale steady light on its crown that Cael does not look at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md:14:- **Standing defaults:** season-blind; feet, yards, paces, strides, cords; nineteen, no birthday; no possessive before "Path" in narration; no new proper names (the factor unnamed); owner-pending protected lines verbatim and unglossed (#52 falls due before or in this movement: confirm its line, if present, is word for word).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/audit-notes.md-15-- **Rule on EVERY flag in AUTHOR-REPORT.md "Owner flags"**, with chapter:line on both sides and a recommendation.
