editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-162-**#50 update (coordinator, 2026-10-11, before B7 Movement 7).** Default confirmed and written into Movement 7's packet: the line stays verbatim and unglossed; no six-year event is invented; the case's twelve years is not stated in that scene. One thing the owner may like to know: the closed Movement 5 has Seln date the registry's survey of the circles at "five years ago by the stake, maybe six" (ch34), so on the page "six years" can be heard as the time since that survey without any change. If the owner prefers option (1) or (2), it is a one-numeral change.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-163-
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-164-## 51. Book 7 — "Tomorrow makes three" (OWNER ITEM; coordinator default in force, 2026-10-11)
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-165-The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-166-- Related, NOT an owner item: the restored protected line "I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board" beside Oryn at Millrace (one day south of Lowmarch) on day 113 was resolved by the owner on 2026-09-04 (EXC-B7-003: "her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days"; BOOK_MAP lists it under "do not reopen"). Movement 7's packet carries a binding note.
