editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-175-## 56–58. Book 8 — three more protected-text items from the final plan re-run (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-176-Source: `book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-H-RERUN.md` (Sol) and `B7-RECONCILIATION-COORDINATOR-OVERRIDES.md`. Sol's list proposed new wording for these protected lines; the coordinator held them back, because no standing decision covers them. Each stays word for word until the owner rules.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-177-- **#56 (Book 8 Movement 2 or 3, Thornwater).** `"Five months and twenty days."` — Lira's arm, from the Ring to its release. It is true on the plan's day count (day 96 to day 265–266) but only if a month is thirty days, and #35 says the prose never states month lengths. **Default:** verbatim. Options: keep; "A hundred and seventy days."; or a wording without a figure.
editions/monroe-1.3/OWNER-DECISIONS.md-178-- **#57 (Book 8 Movements 8–9; extends #49).** Three protected lines speak of Cael's "Path" or say the machine never lit for him: `Because every other site, my Path worked while everyone's died.`; `His Path did not die. It also did not notice it should have.` (narration); `a machine that lit for everyone but him` (narration). Edition canon since Book 6: he has no Path; his own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, and it went dark. **Default:** verbatim; nothing else in the book says "his Path". The two narration lines are the hardest to square, since they are not Cael's own shorthand. Options: release the clauses for a minimal canon repair (Sol drafted wording, kept in the re-run report); or keep as is.
