editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1234-- **Ch1 closing log (270th):** "The ferry runs when the ice goes. Karis has a bearing, an index she can't read, and a language she can't read, and she says the answers are in a border archive nobody's opened since before the Compact. Since my Kindling I've stayed out of registries because a registry is where they file you. She wants me to walk into the oldest one on the continent. The kit reads everyone but me. So does the world, mostly. Nineteen. Ice goes next week. West, and inside, for the first time since the academy above Ostrand — which is a sentence I did not think I'd write again." [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] And the 168th: "Claim: something. Evidence: a cord, two edges, a hair. Ruling: hold."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1235-- **Thornwater:** "Five months and twenty days." [OWNER-pending #56] / "That's a season. Take it off." / "Will you mend it." / "Lie still" / "It's an arm. Use it. It'll be slow for a month and it'll ache in the wet for a year and then it won't. Don't fall on it." / "I don't know what that is." … "Neither do you. Write that down too."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1236-- **S2 doorway:** "You came through the board," / "I came through the board." / "Then you already know it doesn't care who you were." / "I'm learning," Vastin said. **S2 close:** "Because a council would file it," Vastin said, "and I spent forty years being the man they sent to make sure the filing held. I know exactly how deep a thing has to be buried before no one goes looking. This is deeper than that." … "I helped bury smaller things. I'd like to dig one up before I'm done." Also: "Not that. Not for some months. Vastin will do; it did for my father." / "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." / "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1237-- **S4 lesson and log:** "The wall held the line," … "And someone else had to be the reason they wanted the line." … "I have never once in forty years needed someone else to be the reason." / "You do now," / "I know fields. I don't know packs." … "I'll learn or I won't." Log: "Vastin fought. He rooted the road and nearly got eaten for it — a wall's no good if you're the only thing making noise behind it. He knows fields. He doesn't know packs. He'll learn or he won't. Watched an Iron Wall go up two feet from me. Filed it. Note the day: an Archmarshal took a wound out here and there was no one to report it to. He looked almost free. Almost."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md:1238:- **S5:** "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell." … "Draft nothing. Just look." / "Two copies of one ignorance." Close: "Six years," Karis said. "They measured all of it. They graded it — the sites are ranked by something, and it's the same something in the kit, and I can't read either one." … "Everything I can't read points at the same place." / "Treswick," / "The archive under it. Cleon." / "Who's Cleon?" / "The only historical-Path practitioner registered west of the Line. If the language is anywhere, it's under his hands. A day and a half." … "And then I find out whether I've been right for five years or wrong for five years, and I don't know which I'm more afraid of." [OWNER-pending #52]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1239-- **S6:** "I'm not an archive person." / "Leaving and routing are different verbs. I'm doing the second." / "You go inside, you don't go near the station. Not the steps, not the square. You promise me in that log of yours, because I've seen what the log does to you." / the log entry: "The fork. Oryn north; five holds; routing, not the other verb. Her term, given at the fire, taken in the log because that's the form she'll take it in: inside Treswick I do not go near the station. Not the steps. Not the square. Written here so she can read it, and so I can." / "Bring me whatever walks out of that archive with you. All of it." / "Not the steps," … "Not the square."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md-1240-- **S7 log:** "Ran the reading on myself again. Same nothing at the center. I think the reading can't do it — you can't measure a stillness with a thing that only feels movement. I need an instrument for what doesn't move. Karis says there's a man in Treswick who reads how things are built. Maybe that's the instrument. Maybe I'm about to hand a stranger the one question I've never let anyone hold. Tomorrow. The walls are close enough now to have a color." ("color" stands in the log, per ruling 19.) Also: "You were the instrument," … "I was the error." / "I declined to read you a second time. You know that. What you do not know is why."
