editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-003/plan-audit-prompt.md-28-- **The spring (the 280th).** Three readers (Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure). "Behaves as device. Cannot be." — whose remark, on which paper, and does anyone interpret it? Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule and never finishes it. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites in the office's SHEETS, the fourth's twice the size (the field stakes carry it on thirty-two and thirty-four only — coordinator ruling after Movement 1); it stays unread; nobody says who graded the sites or why. **The date:** the second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands; Seln sets the technician's sheet before him without a word; Cael reads a Compact date and knows it for the day of his own Kindling. **No figures are printed (OWNER #60), no span of years is computed (#18), nothing is said or written, and nobody interprets the sequence.** Flag any line that prints a number for the date, counts years, has anyone say the sum, or joins the date to the layer "running". This is the first thing Seln has ever taught anyone (the "Draft nothing. Just look." exchange): confirm he taught nothing earlier in the movement. Seln's locked case stays shut.
